    title: "The Boxer Born of Frogs and Manga",
    body: "Yonago City, Tottori Prefecture. Sena Irie was drawn to boxing by the manga \"Ganbare Genki.\" Captivated by the protagonist who fought with nothing but his fists, she walked into a local gym as an elementary school student.\n\nHer other great passion was frogs. She kept frogs at home and observed their behavior as a daily ritual. \"A frog stays perfectly still before it jumps, storing all its energy. I want to be like that.\" This unique sensibility shaped her boxing style.\n\nShe loved repetitive, fundamental drills more than anyone, throwing the same punch thousands of times. Nothing flashy, but her punches found their mark with surgical precision. She enrolled at Nippon Sport Science University and became a rising name in amateur boxing.",
