    id: "sc-090", athlete_id: "irie", order: 5, stage: "rebirth",
    title: "The First Olympic Gold Medal in Japanese Women's Boxing",
    body: "The first Olympic gold medal in the history of Japanese women's boxing. It was won by the girl from Tottori Prefecture who always said, \"I don't have talent.\"\n\n\"Her strength is that beneath her seemingly timid exterior lies an absolutely unbreakable core.\" (Coach)\n\nInspired by the manga \"Ganbare Genki,\" she started boxing. She learned life philosophy from frogs. She clawed her way up from the depths of a devastating slump to stand atop the Olympic podium. Sena Irie's story is the exhilarating underdog tale of someone who seized the world title with \"effort\" as her only weapon.\n\nWith the gold medal around her neck, the first thing Irie hugged was a stuffed frog. \"Like a frog, I stored my energy, and then I leaped.\" Her smile was the brightest of all.",
